for the co-stars of actors who died  showing up to work without the person  you've been acting alongside for years  can be tragic  these actors were never quite the same  after their co-stars died  john belushi's death in 1982 was a  tragedy for his fans and the many people  who'd been lucky enough to work with him  but none of his former co-stars took the  loss harder than dan aykroyd eckroyd and  belushi worked side by side for years  and whether they were performing on  saturday night live or making music as  the blues brothers the two were an  unbeatable comedy duo decades after  belushi's death aykroyd still wishes  that somehow things had gone differently  for belushi  later in life ackroyd co-founded a chain  of music venues called the house of  blues  and aykroyd has publicly wished that  belushi was still around to be a part of  it  aykroyd said in an interview with the  guardian i think about him every damn  time i walk into a house of blues  why aren't you here man to enjoy all  this when chadwick boseman died at the  age of 43 from colon cancer his fans  were stunned  for boseman's black panther co-stars the  loss was overwhelming  michael b jordan who played killmonger  opposite bozeman's black panther was  deeply affected by boseman's death  during a 2020 interview with vanity fair  jordan said when reflecting on what he'd  learned  you want to do the most you can and get  the most out of the time that you have  uh and make it count while there is a  sequel to black panther in the works  currently scheduled for release in 2022  it won't be the same without bozeman  while starting in luke cage mike coulter  had the opportunity to work alongside  reggie kathy an accomplished actor who  was widely known for playing norman  wilson in the critically acclaimed drama  the wire  kathy was diagnosed with lung cancer  while they shot season 2  and died in february 2018 before the  season was released  although their time together on the show  was short coulter felt a genuine kinship  with kathy  coulter said during a panel at baltimore  comic con in 2018  reg was great i wish we got a chance to  spend more time together it was like  discovering a friend you didn't get a  chance to really hang out with i don't  know how he did it  coming on set physically being  completely worn out but at the same time  giving 100  in april 2020 the news broke that actor  sam lloyd had died just over a year  after being diagnosed with a brain tumor  and lung cancer  best known for his role as the nervous  lawyer ted on scrubs  lloyd had gotten married shortly before  his diagnosis and he and his wife  vanessa had welcomed their first child  despite his serious diagnosis lloyd's  loved ones and former co-stars hoped  that he would heal somehow  not long before his death lloyd's fellow  scrubs cast member zac braf ran into him  and thought he might be recovering  raff said in an interview with extra it  was just such a a sad story because he  was sick  just when he had like found true love  and had a baby it was just  such a sad story in july 2020 the death  of naya rivera  shocked glee fans who finally remembered  rivera for playing the witty and  ruthless cheerleader santana lopez in  the musical comedy series  rivera drowned while swimming with her  son josie and fans poured out their  condolences to her fellow gleek cast  members who were mourning her death not  only was jane lynch grieving over  rivera's death but she also stated that  her niece megan was close with rivera as  well  leaving the two of them struggling to  come to terms with what had happened  months later jane lynch who had played  sue sylvester on the series reflected on  the loss to access hollywood you could  have no better friend than naya rivera  the news of robin williams's death in  2014 shocked everyone  it was hard to believe that the man who  had spent decades making everyone laugh  was gone  matt damon who had worked with williams  on the academy award-winning film  goodwill hunting was particularly  affected by the loss  damon said that he felt that he owed his  success to williams and there was no way  for him to repay williams for taking a  chance on working with him and ben  affleck on goodwill hunting  he was regretful that he had fallen out  of touch with williams in the years  leading up to his death  damon said in an interview with yahoo  news i think everyone who wasn't there  with him at the end feels bad that they  didn't see it coming i hope i become  better at checking in with my friends  and i hope that we as a country get  better at checking in with each other to  prevent this kind of thing stand by me  is a classic 80s film and the cast grew  close while filming  but after shooting rapt will wheaton  river phoenix corey feldman and jerry  o'connell went their own separate ways  less than a decade after its release  phoenix died of a drug overdose and many  years later wheaton reflected  i didn't feel a real sense of loss at  the time the river i knew and loved had  been gone for a long time at that point  but i felt sad for his family and angry  at the people around him who didn't do  more to help him help himself  25 years after the release of stand by  me the cast reunited for a commemorative  blu-ray edition of the movie wheaton  said he finally felt the full impact of  river's death at this reunion that's  what it took to make his death and his  absence a real thing that i could feel  instead of an event that i wasn't a part  of but i'm forced to talk about more  often than i'd like  but despite feeling intense grief  wheaton was grateful for the reunion and  the realizations it brought to him he  just wished that river could have been  there too  leonard nimoy and william shatner worked  side by side on star trek playing spock  and captain kirk  they were friends for many years yet  they eventually grew apart and the two  actors even stopped speaking  but when nimoy died in 2015 shatner  admitted that they'd never mended their  friendship in an interview with the new  york daily news shatner said  until the day i die i will still wonder  what caused that rift after all the  years we had spent together after the  bond we had forged  what could i have done that was so  irreparable that he couldn't even talk  to me about it i just don't know and  it's sad and it's permanent  i don't know why he stopped talking to  me when the news broke that soprano star  james gandolfini had died in rome after  suffering a heart attack his fellow cast  members were devastated  tony soprano is an iconic tv character  and nearly two decades after the finale  aired there's no denying that the  sopranos has had a lasting influence on  prestige tv  after hearing about gandalfini's death  his co-star lorraine bronco who played  tony's therapist dr melfi  felt like she needed to take this moment  as a wake-up call she decided that she  had to turn her life around and start  practicing healthier habits  bronco connected with a friend who had  similar goals and the two embarked  on the journey together she ended up  writing a book about the experience  titled to the fullest the clean up your  act plan to lose weight rejuvenate and  be the best you can be  lauren mccall and humphrey bogart were  two of the biggest stars of the classic  hollywood film era it almost seemed like  fate that they would eventually fall in  love  after working together on the film to  have and have nots in 1944 sparks were  flying which was somewhat complicated by  the fact that bogart was married at the  time  shortly after the film premiered bogart  divorced his wife and married mccall  just a few months later  sadly after just over a decade of  marriage with mccall bogart died in 1957  both bacall and bogart famously had  affairs while married to each other but  their chemistry was still undeniable  mccall did remarry a few years after  bogart's death he had her second husband  jason robart still referred to her as  the widow bogart she never truly got  over bogart and in her memoir be myself  mccall wrote no one has ever written a  romance better than we lived  beloved actor philip seymour hoffman  tragically overdosed and died in 2014  among the countless peers who mourned  him was george clooney who worked with  hoffman on his film the ice of march  in an interview with abc news clooney  stated that the last time he saw hoffman  was a few months before his death  the two had dinner together in berlin  and clooney noticed that hoffman wasn't  quite acting like himself but he didn't  realize just how much his friend was  struggling  he seemed to have been having a tougher  time you know and there's no  understanding what goes on in an  individual's mind in their lives  when disney channel star cameron boyce  passed away after a fatal seizure it was  a harrowing wake-up call for his  co-stars  boyce died young he was only 20 and he  should have had an amazing life and  career ahead of him  his descendants co-stars couldn't  believe that he was gone dove cameron  who played mal and considered boyce a  close friend said that his death  reminded the cast just how precious life  is  cameron explained to today i think  that's kind of how we're all feeling is  we want to make an effort it really  reminds you how important everybody is  how important your one life is cameron  also got a tattoo to remember boyce  she chose a design with a flower coming  out of a gun an international symbol for  peace and anti-war movements  she stated that boyce was working with  an organization against gun violence  before his death and she wanted to  memorialize him as someone who cared  deeply about peace  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite celebrities are coming  soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you

